# Testing & Benchmarks

- Unit: Vitest for Core and for `@dndgem/dom` measurement (mocked geometry / fake `ResizeObserver`) and drag interaction (fake mechanics).
- Browser/E2E: Playwright Chromium smoke (playground boot + DND-1.6 drag fixture + DND-1.7 Vanilla/React integration + DND-1.8 cancel/resize proofs); broader product surfaces later.
- Property-based testing: DND-1.3 uses table-driven Vitest; defer fast-check until justified.
- Benchmarks (DND-1.8): Core `solveLayout` suites under `benchmarks/` via `pnpm bench`. Deterministic fixtures only. Absolute timings are hardware-dependent evidence, not universal guarantees. Framework adapters must not alter Core semantics to improve numbers.

## Private Technical MVP quality gates

- GitHub CI: browser smoke only (`pnpm test:e2e` + smoke prerequisites).
- Sprint Final Quality Gate (local, mandatory before sprint complete / final commit/push):
  `lint`, `format:check`, `typecheck`, `test`, `build`, `check:boundaries`,
  playground + example builds, `test:e2e`, and `bench`.
- See `docs/architecture/testing-strategy.md`. CI may be strengthened before Public Alpha.
